{
  // MODE-DIVERGENCE REGISTRY - tooling only, NOT built into dist/overlay.json
  //
  // WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
  // tarkov.dev derives one game mode's numbers from the other for some tasks,
  // and the direction it mirrors can flip. Overrides that only pin the mode
  // that happens to be broken today silently become both redundant AND
  // insufficient when the mirror reverses - which is exactly what happened to
  // the PvE experience overrides (see git history for src/overrides/modes/pve).
  //
  // This registry records verified TRUE values per upstream mode so a mirror
  // flip is detectable. `npm run check-overrides` compares the effective
  // merged value per mode against these entries and reports which overrides are
  // currently load-bearing versus currently redundant. A converged entry is
  // retained only while upstream is still wrong or an override actively guards
  // the recorded truth. Once both authoritative sources and upstream agree and
  // no override remains, the record is retired to git history rather than kept
  // as inert registry data.
  //
  // SOURCES OF TRUTH
  //   pve      -> `in-game`: PvE values verified in-game on the PvE profile
  //               (read off the quest screens). PvE is the mode we verify
  //               directly, so it is treated as authoritative here.
  //   regular  -> `wiki` when the page is current, `patch-notes` when the
  //               wiki still documents a pre-1.1 figure: the Season 1 patch
  //               notes state the task-reward rebalance applies to ALL game
  //               modes (PvP Season, PvP Zone, PvE Zone), and the 1.1-pve
  //               data carries single mode-free values (gameMode filters in
  //               quest data are edition gates only, never
  //               regular/pve/pvp-season), so a 1.1 figure verified in PvE
  //               applies to the other modes unless a per-mode split is
  //               documented.
  //   pvp-season -> `patch-notes`: same all-modes 1.1 rework evidence;
  //               not independently verified in-game.
  //
  // STATUS
  //   divergent      - the two modes genuinely differ in-game; both values pinned
  //   converged      - all recorded modes currently share one verified value
  //   mode-exclusive - task only exists in one mode; no cross-mode comparison

  // MODE-EXCLUSIVE - task exists in only one mode, so no mirror can occur.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  // Easy Money - Part 2
  '6834158f2f0e2a7eb90b62c8': {
    name: 'Easy Money - Part 2',
    proof: 'https://escapefromtarkov.fandom.com/wiki/Easy_Money_-_Part_2',
    status: 'mode-exclusive',
    note: 'PvE-only task; absent from the regular-mode task list entirely.',
    fields: {
      experience: {
        pve: 2900,
        confidence: 'high',
        pveSource: 'in-game',
        verified: 'in-game',
      },
    },
  },

